<title>USA: USDA says signup for livestock aid June 30-July 25.</title>
<headline>USDA says signup for livestock aid June 30-July 25.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said the sign-up period for aid for livestock farmers who suffered losses from recent natural disasters, including brutal blizzards in the Dakotas, will run from June 30 -July 25.</p>
<p>The $50 million program will make direct payments to producers to help cover part of the market value for the animals lost. The fund were authorized in the disaster aid bill signed into law by President Clinton on June 12.</p>
